# Allowlist ONLY these hosts. One host per line, matched as an FQDN
# (see tinyproxy.conf: FilterExtended On).
# 1. The upstream Metro Train GTFS-Realtime gateway (2a).
^api\.opendata\.transport\.vic\.gov\.au$
# 2. The external dead-man's-switch ping target (2b) — deliberate, narrow
# widening confirmed by Ronnie 2026-07-21, not the default upstream host.
^hc-ping\.com$
# 3. The static GTFS schedule portal (2c/05a) — deliberately the PLAIN
# host, not the `api.` gateway above: this is a different, unauthenticated
# CKAN endpoint on the same parent domain. Confirmed 2026-07-31 this is the
# actual download host, not a redirect target — see 05a session notes for
# the live-container verification this line depends on.
^opendata\.transport\.vic\.gov\.au$
# 4. Anthropic API (05b) — Haiku calls from ai/llm_client.py.
^api\.anthropic\.com$
# 5. Langfuse Cloud (05b-iii) — matches the actual configured
# LANGFUSE_BASE_URL value, not assumed; confirmed 2026-07-31.
^cloud\.langfuse\.com$
# 6. Slack incoming webhooks (05e) — fixed host regardless of which
# webhook/workspace/channel TT_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL actually points at (also
# now used by the poller directly, not just Grafana — see docker-compose.yml).
^hooks\.slack\.com$
# 7. Flagsmith remote-evaluation API (feature-toggle system) — SaaS default
# host; only the api service's process calls this (flags/client.py), not
# the poller. Added ahead of real key generation; verify still correct once
# a Flagsmith environment actually exists.
^edge\.api\.flagsmith\.com$
# 8. Hugging Face archive pipeline (M9) — huggingface_hub's real upload
# path hits TWO hosts, not one: the main API, and a separate "xet"
# storage/CDN backend that actually carries the file bytes. Confirmed by
# routing a real (test) upload through a logging proxy 2026-08-07 rather
# than guessed — a single-hostname filter would have silently broken real
# uploads. Only the archiver service calls these, not the poller.
^huggingface\.co$
^cas-server\.xethub\.hf\.co$
